      "result": "W",
      "result_description": "Wadebridge CC - 1st XI - Won",
      "result_applied_to": "36578",
      "match_notes": "Wadebridge maintained their lead at the top on what turned out to be an historic day for the team, who amassed 375-8 and won by 311 runs, both thought to be club records. Their mammoth score was centred around a maiden 1st XI hundred from Charlie McLachlan, whose 171 off 142 balls was made in a century second-wicket partnership with Matt Jolliffe (36) and a rapid double-hundred stand with Cal Morse (81) for the third wicket. In reply, Gorran's only option was to go for their shots, but a flurry of outside edges saw Stuart Parkyn (5-36) and Barny Jackson (2-17) bundle them out for only 64.",
